SOUNDDVR device-3 (OPL) NOTE methods + note-play chain: driver-DS rebase so the voice-reset + note-on
paths complete faithfully (the OPL key-on/off + frequency writes reach out(0x388)).

After patch 353 selects device 3 and runs the OPL init, the device-select's voice-reset tail
(0c94 -> 0ca9 -> 0aa7 -> `jmp *[ds:0x1a5]` = device-3 slot3 = 10e3) and the note-play dispatch reach the
device-3 per-voice OPL methods, which were the next driver-DS base-loss (SIGSEGV in 10e3 at host 0xc01).
All asm-verified vs re_out/fist_snd_image.bin:

  * 10e3 - device-3 per-voice KEY-ON/OFF (regs 0x40/0xB0); param_3 = voice (BX at the 0aa7 tail-jmp).
  * 10a6 - device-3 channel FREQUENCY (regs 0xA0/0xB0).
  * 0aa7 - restore the velocity scale the tail method reads in CL (asm 0xab6-0xac1: cl=high((cl*2)*
           voice[0xfd])); patch 351 had omitted it (its tail then went to device-0 null).  Pass the live
           AX/CX/BX to the tail device method faithfully (BX = voice).
  * 0966 - note dispatch: [ds:0x13e2] note-table base + the two note-table passes.
  * 0997 - note-ON: free-voice scan + note-record read + 0cfb (freq/env) + 0aa7 (key-on).  Ghidra aliased
           the voice index / record pointer; reconstructed from asm.
  * 0cfb - load the voice freq/env from the per-instrument tables driver_ds:0x15b4/0xfc9/0x10d4/0x152e/
           0x14ac; tail `jmp *[ds:0x1c1]` = device-3 slot5 = 0f99 (NEAR).

Reached only under FIST_SB (device 3 is selected only when the FIST_SB-gated config path threads letter
'C'); the default boot never dispatches here -> zero effect on the 26 video flows.
